e\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c490373889e9f00494d7ccc5b096cdfc97b2a59968521ddcfcb893f65ed98779","event_uuid":"7b2ea848-0a9f-4d7a-b0e2-2b66b67b4c94","position":{"commit_sha":"2d0582412eec43f05e3bee8f4984ab21292f209b","position":"1787061837435715001-7b2ea848-0a9f-4d7a-b0e2-2b66b67b4c94"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6ba095adabb11aa0cae0802952b4306a390cc779373f2987e85ec46970413967","event_uuid":"3ccba811-472d-4f9f-b95a-fea505f12249","position":{"commit_sha":"0ad29a335195d279609c3548015d5d347d9d0fb2","position":"1787061864690584001-3ccba811-472d-4f9f-b95a-fea505f12249"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"029e86a3c09e571d452a3c342d44644810b7c7889de954bbe3fea250849d93e4","event_uuid":"6e7b45f2-3d82-4a45-b3bd-cbe366b8f975","position":{"commit_sha":"56f292b4dbe4e644597fe9aec63684ee016938c9","position":"1787062236753741001-6e7b45f2-3d82-4a45-b3bd-cbe366b8f975"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c00838245082930680bd717fcd33f0d5e8948dd7ca8413b0c6171d1f1cf02e65","event_uuid":"4aead3f9-80ed-41cc-b5de-31d1d35d4fcf","position":{"commit_sha":"612f80d3ad9a211db9eb4b1ce1ee7db01a202384","position":"1787062241519944001-4aead3f9-80ed-41cc-b5de-31d1d35d4fcf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA — CONFIRMED DEFECT\n\nProven root cause: commit d9e0f0e733 replaced `_commit_binding_store_snapshot`’s package-independent stdlib subprocess calls with `from rebar_reconciler import git_adapter`. After the mechanical d0e65c0e03 extraction, that import is `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py:200`. In explicitly supported standalone mode, `reconcile.py:20-36` bootstraps only the dotted loader key and loads the helper under flat key `reconcile_helpers` at :51-64; `reconcile_helpers.py:30-46` likewise bootstraps the loader but does not create a parent `rebar_reconciler` package. Calling the re-export therefore raises at line 200 before the no-files `True` branch (:219-221) and before the fail-open catch (:223-253).\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof: a fresh raw `reconcile.py` load completed with `_helpers.__name__ == \"reconcile_helpers\"`, no parent package, and the loader key present. An execution trace entered only helper line 200, emitted `ModuleNotFoundError`, and never reached lines 219-223. Exact historical probes returned `True` at d9^, became red at d9, and stayed red across d0^, d0, pre-RP-04 4c3e5970e6, and current HEAD, rejecting extraction/RP-04 as causes. The raw failure had zero git_adapter module objects; the supported package route returned `True` and had exactly one `rebar_reconciler.git_adapter` object, rejecting cache/identity duplication. The engine_env subprocess route was also green. A catch-only counterfactual returned `False` even with no files; adding a literal no-file preflight restored `True` but a real-git/existing-binding input still returned `False`, proving catch widening is only symptom containment, not restoration of the standalone sibling contract.\n\nLegitimacy: `defect`. `reconcile_helpers.py:10-16,30-46` and `reconcile.py:20-36,51-58` explicitly promise by-path standalone execution, `_loader.py:1-29` documents no-package sibling loading, and `_commit_binding_store_snapshot` explicitly promises `True` for nothing-to-commit and fail-open `False` for operational failure. Pre-d9 runtime proves this behavior existed. The strongest not-a-bug case (public package routes are green) is rejected because test/back-compat standalone behavior is an explicit maintained contract, not filer expectation.\n\nExpected post-fix behavior: a standalone-loaded helper resolves git_adapter through the existing sibling loader under canonical key `rebar_reconciler.git_adapter`, reaches the same True/False commit-back semantics, and shares the package-context adapter object when one is pre-seeded. Bounded caller sweep: one production definition, one reconcile re-export, one production call after binding-store save, plus direct tests; all depend on a bool result and none depend on the import failure. No behavioral dependency blocks repair.","timestamp":1787052295887532001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report\n\nProblem: a package-free by-path load of reconcile.py raised ModuleNotFoundError when its re-exported binding-store commit helper ran.\n\nProven root cause: d9e0f0e733 changed the helper from package-independent git calls to an unconditional top-level rebar_reconciler.git_adapter import at reconcile_helpers.py:200. Standalone reconcile.py creates the loader child key and loads reconcile_helpers under a flat key, but does not create an importable parent package, so execution failed before the documented no-state True branch and fail-open catch.\n\nProof: the fresh-process trace entered line 200 and raised with find_spec(rebar_reconciler) returning None; it never reached the result branches. The exact historical probe was True at d9 parent and red from d9 onward. Package and engine_env routes stayed green, ruling out adapter behavior. Catch-widening experiments returned the wrong no-state result and could not perform commit-back, ruling out containment as repair.\n\nTest: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_reconcile_helpers_standalone_git_adapter.py was collected and executed RED first under the CI marker gate. Its three isolated python -I subprocess cases all failed at the exact ModuleNotFoundError. The file was physically removed before the blind fixer ran, then restored GREEN at 3 passed. Re-seeding the exact old absolute import returned all three to RED; restoring the repair returned all three to GREEN. The oracle asserts return values, canonical adapter identity, adapter-boundary calls, and stderr diagnostics, so it is behavior-focused and refactor-tolerant.\n\nFix: _commit_binding_store_snapshot now resolves git_adapter through the existing _load helper with canonical key rebar_reconciler.git_adapter and sibling file git_adapter.py. This restores package-free loading while preserving cache/preseed identity and every existing git operation and True/False/error behavior.\n\nScope and safety: bounded callers are the reconcile.py re-export, one production call after binding-store save, and direct tests; none depended on the import failure. The fix restores pre-d9 behavior, adds no dependency or capability, and weakens no existing test. Only one production line and the held-out regression module changed.\n\nSiblings: the construct sweep covered every remaining absolute git_adapter import. The advisory-lock and ref-lock standalone defects are already repaired/tracked by fibrous-fabulous-dungbeetle; _concurrency is dispositioned by the pending design-classification ticket silt-resistant-gonolek; apply_outbound.py and __main__.py are package-context-only and are not siblings. No new undispositioned construct hit remains. Parity rule: binding-store snapshot commit-back preserves its boolean/error contract in package and standalone loading contexts. CLI and automated reconciliation converge through __main__.py:534 -> reconcile_once -> reconcile.py:668 -> this helper. MCP/API and public library expose no independent snapshot operation; there is no mirror-direction operation requiring the loader rule. No MISSING parity slot.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: unit-suite package pollution could mask this class; fixed in scope by the isolated python -I contract test. No other observed fragility remains undispositioned.\n\nReplication and gates: the exact fresh-process package-free reproduction now prints True. Focused helper/state tests: 10 passed. Full state suite: 355 passed. Full reconciler unit suite: 2775 passed. make lint passed, make typecheck passed, commit hooks passed, and local rebar review-code returned PASS with 0 blocking and 0 advisory findings. Commit a4309975d04e3528c8eb863383ebc7591a31610f carries DCO, Change-Id I2685bc10db4d2114b585fda4c6fd9feef4947b3c, and the canonical ticket trailer. Not pushed or closed while Change 1855 owns the serialized CI slot.","timestamp":1787053556021976001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landing update: rebased commit 2935b17701264a56f133c2fc44609829d0e27168 onto current main, reran the held-out standalone oracle (3 passed), make lint, and make typecheck. Gerrit Change 1858 run 32142714245 passed every executed lane in 1956 seconds with no retry; Gerrit recorded LLM-Review+1, Verified+1, and zero unresolved comments. Change 1858 merged as 2935b17701264a56f133c2fc44609829d0e27168.","timestamp":1787061837435715001}],"created_at":1787047761822012001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"604ed2bf-a39a-409f-9aae-305cd65068a6","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"79c6-eaf3-38af-4ce9"},{"link_uuid":"d4d21c2f-7e5f-496c-bc2a-722a6b24d529","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"36cc-18d5-c984-4ecd"},{"link_uuid":"3f8366ec-de0f-42be-80b0-901a22b37aa2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d111-91e6-28da-4ff4"}],"description":"## Context\n`reconcile_helpers.py` explicitly supports standalone file-path execution and bootstraps the shared sibling loader, but `_commit_binding_store_snapshot()` unconditionally imports `git_adapter` through the absent top-level package. `reconcile.py` loads the helper by path under flat key `reconcile_helpers`, so the supported standalone path raises `ModuleNotFoundError` before the helper can return its documented `True`/`False` result.\n\n## Confirmed Root Cause\nCommit `d9e0f0e733` replaced package-independent subprocess calls with `from rebar_reconciler import git_adapter`. Runtime tracing proves the import fails at `reconcile_helpers.py:200` with no parent package and before the no-file or fail-open branches. Exact historical probes are green at d9^ and red from d9 through current HEAD. `reconcile_helpers.py:10-16,30-46`, `reconcile.py:20-36,51-58`, and `_loader.py:1-29` are the authoritative standalone contract.\n\n## Repair Plan\n- Replace the package-dependent import with the existing sibling loader using canonical key `rebar_reconciler.git_adapter` and file `git_adapter.py`.\n- Preserve the helper’s current no-file `True`, successful-commit `True`, and operational-failure `False` plus diagnostic semantics.\n- Preserve module identity: a package-context/pre-seeded adapter and the standalone helper must resolve the same canonical `sys.modules` object.\n- Keep the change confined to the helper import seam and one held-out regression module; add no dependency and do not alter git operation behavior.\n\n## Testing\n- Add `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_reconcile_helpers_standalone_git_adapter.py` and first run it RED on the current source with `pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_reconcile_helpers_standalone_git_adapter.py`.\n- After the blind repair, rerun that held-out file GREEN, seed the exact old absolute-import defect and require it to return RED, then restore the repair and require GREEN.\n- Run `pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_commit_binding_store_failure.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_retired_commit.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_reconcile_helpers_standalone_git_adapter.py`.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck` with this worktree’s `.venv/bin` first on `PATH`.\n- Replicate the original fresh-process, package-free `reconcile.py` call against a temporary repository and confirm the helper returns through its documented contract.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A package-free by-path load of `reconcile.py` calls the re-exported commit helper without `ModuleNotFoundError`.\n- [x] A no-state standalone commit-back returns `True`.\n- [x] A standalone commit-back with state files reaches the canonical adapter’s git operations.\n- [x] Package-context and standalone execution reuse one `sys.modules[\"rebar_reconciler.git_adapter\"]` module object.\n- [x] A simulated git failure returns `False` and emits the documented binding-store diagnostic.\n- [x] The focused helper/state suite passes under the stated `pytest` command.\n- [x] `make lint` passes.\n- [x] `make typecheck` passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"Restore the explicit standalone sibling-loading contract by resolving git_adapter through the existing canonical-key lazy loader."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_reconcile_helpers_standalone_git_adapter.py","reason":"Held-out regression oracle for raw reconcile/helper loading, commit-back semantics, and canonical package identity."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","36cc-18d5-c984-4ecd"],["relates_to","d111-91e6-28da-4ff4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6e7b45f2-3d82-4a45-b3bd-cbe366b8f975","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["reconciler","import","bridge"],"ticket_id":"cfe1-3572-4536-49d3","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Standalone reconcile helpers cannot import git adapter","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2606a637-2245-4356-b5d5-e81db712e983","9ffb9e80-f3ec-48cb-862c-6ef0f29bbf5c","59a44755-8794-4086-bede-3327b22ac9f5","7ae22129-b17e-43e2-a98c-e8fee1f1ba1f","70d017c0-24a2-42f2-b303-de3a349c9d3b","88ffd228-1617-4cd6-b37b-6a0f6eb9a88e","d4d21c2f-7e5f-496c-bc2a-722a6b24d529","1753520a-5c58-4c14-a769-f6a74187c9d7","3f8366ec-de0f-42be-80b0-901a22b37aa2","7b2ea848-0a9f-4d7a-b0e2-2b66b67b4c94","3ccba811-472d-4f9f-b95a-fea505f12249","6e7b45f2-3d82-4a45-b3bd-cbe366b8f975","4aead3f9-80ed-41cc-b5de-31d1d35d4fcf"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787065234622725001,"uuid":"5fd0fc0f-c7f6-4c3e-bd30-e0731de0a236"}